# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# KCD, 119.4 min of real streamed gameplay, o:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) through Windows.Graphics.Capture, with the synthesized presents drawn by the optical flow warp and its cut gate with the flow's cost output off (the compositor only, the policy is the default's), through the second capture card, 2026-11-10, build aaca501; cut to the gameplay the stream's video shows, 46.6 s to 7210.0 s
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description KCD, 119.4 min of real streamed gameplay, o:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) through Windows.Graphics.Capture, with the synthesized presents drawn by the optical flow warp and its cut gate with the flow's cost output off (the compositor only, the policy is the default's), through the second capture card, 2026-11-10, build aaca501; cut to the gameplay the stream's video shows, 46.6 s to 7210.0 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 32
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.6
field_pull_wraps 85
# WHAT IT COVERS: the 2026-11-10 stream, 119.4 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows,
# captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture with o:vsync on aaca501 (the flow's cost output off;
# the policy is that of 2044bc4), the fourth stream through the second capture card, its display
# at 60.000199 Hz, and the longest whole stream in the corpus. The game hitched (20 to 100 ms)
# 483 times (243 an hour) and stalled for 100 ms or more 56 times (28 an hour), in 83 bursts, 41
# of them with a stall; the longest stalls are 486 ms at about 318 s and 473 ms at 5922 s and
# 5017 s, and the longest capture gap 517 ms. No periodic stretch. Near the end, 6925 s to 6947 s,
# the game ran at about 40 fps for 22 s while walking a camp at night (86 hitches in two bursts,
# none of them a stall); the worst blend run, 32 presents, starts there at 6926.7 s in both the
# field and the replay, and the second worst, 30, starts at 839.15 s with a lock release. The lock
# released 21 times. Of the 99 moves on the replay, 15 of them late, 18 land more than 2 ms from a
# real frame.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 46.570 s, from the 2645
# marked frames in its first 44 s, all on time within 0.42 ms of that offset (p90). The video
# runs 7167.2 s with no holes; it opens on gameplay and ends on the pause menu, which opens at
# video time 7164.25 s, so the cut is 46.6 s to 7210.0 s (video 0:00 to 1:59:23.4). Inside the
# cut, 51 seconds in 34 runs fall out of the 60 fps regime: 32 hitch runs of one or two seconds
# (33 s) and two runs, 18 s, inside the 22 s night-camp stretch above, which is gameplay.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay line (the plain arm, no dejitter) reads synth 0.5% against 0.6%, worst run 31 against
# 32, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 79 against 85. On the dejitter arm, which is how the
# stream ran, blends are 2362 against 2370, repeats 317 against 316, skips 187 against 187, pull
# wraps 41.7 an hour against 42.7 and the worst run 32 against 32, hence max_worst_run_dejit 32
# beside the plain arm's 31. The replay makes 99 moves, 15 late, and the field's log has 96, 13
# late, in the window. The field's 21 releases and the replay's 22: 19 pair within 0.50 ms, one
# at 839.13 s the replay makes one present later (+17 ms), and the field's 3384.63 s release the
# replay makes twice, at 3383.98 s and 4 presents early at 3384.56 s. The planner line reads 2283
# of 2285 synthesized presents planned by the step against 2199 by a guessed target; in the field
# the window's 2370 synthesized presents were all planned or drawn (2281 warped from a flow handed
# over earlier, 87 drawn as the blend because the flow was handed over at that present, 2
# unplanned, none with no flow).
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 31
max_worst_run_dejit 32
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 0.9
min_reseeds 116
max_pull_wraps 79
compositor interp
extra_lag_ms 75
